Website Testing – Peer Assessment Checklist
Instruction: Highlight in YELLOW any points that meet the standard. Leave
unhighlighted if it needs improvement.

SPRINT 1:
�� Feedback Tips:
 Be specific – say exactly what is good and what needs improvement.
 Use “I” statements – e.g., I found it easy to read the text because…
 Always write one positive and one suggestion for each section.

1. Aesthetics – How does it look?
Contrast – Text is clear and easy to read.
Alignment – Everything is lined up neatly.
Proximity – Related items are close; unrelated items have space.
Consistency – Same fonts, colours, and styles across pages.
Balance – Not too crowded or too empty.
White Space – Enough empty space around text and images.
Score (0–6): 6
Feedback: Everything is easy to read and understand. It’s also laid out nicely with items that relate to each other placed together or near each other without cramping everything into one small area. Though it’s a bit plain, maybe add something to make the page less plain or add other pages so users can explore more in the website rather than just that one page.
___________________________________________________________

2. Functionality – Does it work?
Links – All links work and go to the right place.
Navigation – Menus and buttons take you where expected.
Scrolling – You can scroll without problems.
Page Load – No errors; all images and text appear.
Responsive – Works well on a desktop screen.
Score (0–5): 4
Feedback: The layout and website doesn’t have a problem when being used on a desktop screen and there’s no errors in images and texts. But the link and movies on the homepage doesn’t go to anything so add something after clicking the link so it’s actually working and takes users to the right places.
___________________________________________________________

3. Usability – Is it easy to use?
Readability – Text is big enough and easy to read.
Accessibility – Clear headings, alt text for images, good contrast.
Find Info – Information is easy to find.
User Friendly – Feels welcoming and clear.
Score (0–4): 4

Feedback: The website is very user friendly/welcoming and it is clear where things are within the website. Information is really easy to navigate and the text is good sized therefore reading the text isn’t a problem.
___________________________________________________________

4. Bonus Criteria (Optional)
Purpose – Easy to see what the site is about.
Engaging – Makes you want to explore more.
Spelling – No big spelling or grammar mistakes.
Score (0–3): 2
Feedback: Everything here is good, you can easily tell what the site is about from all the movies visibly presented when you go into it and there’s no mistake in grammar nor spelling, however the biggest issue is that the design or layout of the web page is quite boring for users because it’s quite repetitive but possibly once finished with the entire website it’ll be less boring so it’s recommended to add things like more pages into the website making it more interesting. 
___________________________________________________________






